(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2800005200-kotoba-library-publication-surfaces")
  (:adr/title "Kotoba library publication is CLI-first; language, control, and storage surfaces stay separate")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-29")
  (:adr/related (vector "kotoba-lang/kotoba docs/ADR-kotoba-library-publish-cli.md"
                "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang docs/adr/ADR-library-catalog-publication-boundary.md"
                "kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud docs/adr/0001-kotoba-cloud-control-plane.md"))
  (:adr/body "# Kotoba library publication surfaces\n\n## Decision\n\nLibrary publication begins in `kotoba library`, not in a second web registry. `kotoba library inspect` exposes the definition CID, release-head CID, exact dependency CID edges, names, and optional GitHub provenance without collapsing those identities. `kotoba library publish` is a dry-run by default. Explicit local apply keeps the existing signed namespace-head and IPNS operation; `--hosted` first stores every canonical immutable block in Kotobase, then opens a bounded public request at `kotoba.cloud` for explicit Passkey approval of the locally signed head. The namespace signing key never leaves the CLI.\n\nThe public surfaces have distinct jobs:\n\n- `kotoba-lang.org/libraries/` is the language-owned catalog and comparison surface. It explains supported libraries, exact dependencies, content-addressed identities, provenance, comparison axes, and the hosted publication command.\n- `kotoba.cloud` is the account, authorization, deploy, and publication-control surface. It verifies the exact request under a same-origin Passkey session and relays only the signed record.\n- `kotobase.net` is the storage and retrieval plane for immutable raw or DAG-CBOR blocks and independently verified signed name heads.\n- `itonami.cloud` is the agent-work plane.\n- `murakumo.cloud` is the compute plane, including GPU capacity.\n\n## Implemented truth boundary\n\nHosted Passkey publication is live as of 2026-08-29. Kotobase Worker version `79cf4ced-233a-4609-a137-9cc45fe78aa6` accepts authenticated canonical DAG-CBOR/sha2-256 blocks while rejecting unsupported codecs. Kotoba Cloud version `a39f4880-a564-4fa0-9a6b-8ee542fa6884` publishes `POST /v1/libraries/publish`, requires exact same-origin plus a valid `gftd_session`, rejects unsigned or mismatched fields, and forwards neither the Passkey cookie nor ambient authorization to Kotobase. Kotoba language site version `866d733c-4aa8-4f07-9e82-549ab5422d46` publishes the English/Japanese catalog and machine-readable discovery document.\n\nThe returned receipt is immediate evidence bound to the stable principal, active DID, namespace, release CID, record CID, publisher, and time. Durable publication history, catalog ingestion from receipts, revocation UI, and a short-lived Passkey-scoped storage grant remain follow-up work. The CLI therefore still needs a storage write-token file for block ingress. SourceCID, BuildCID, ArtifactCID, semantic definition CID, release-head CID, record CID, and mutable aliases remain different identifiers.\n\n## User path\n\n`inspect -> locally sign -> store immutable blocks -> open kotoba.cloud approval URL -> approve with Passkey -> receive bound receipt -> discover in catalog`. Web pages explain and verify this path; they do not replace the CLI signature or make the control plane the storage authority.")))
